# Desktop UI

The editor is one column: head, then a row, then the timeline.

```tsx
<div className="desktop">
  <header className="head">{/* project bar only */}</header>
  <div className="workspace">
    <div className="library">{/* rail + assets */}</div>
    <div className="center">{/* preview + transport */}</div>
    <aside className="inspector" />
  </div>
  <Timeline />
</div>
```

Separate panels with a dark gap (`#141414`), not a border. The gap is the drag handle. A `#141414` hairline may split a region inside a panel. It is not a drag handle. `#1c1c1c` is the library, preview, inspector, and timeline. `#262626` is the project bar. Editor text does not select. Fields still do.

Keep those gaps. The preview absorbs the leftover space.

Icons come from `@hugeicons/core-free-icons` through `src/editor/icons.tsx`. Do not draw new UI icons, and do not import a Hugeicons Pro package. The blade mark in that file is the only custom glyph.

A slider is a 4px track and a plain white round thumb. No border, box, or focus outline on the control. A color grade may paint the track. The thumb stays white.

Hovering a tool, a clip, a marker, a library card, or an icon button shows its name in a tooltip. A clip also shows its time span. The tip sits above the control.
